# Locus of Enlightenment: "Whenever you activate an ability that isn't a mana ability, copy it." Any ability its controller
# activates, of any source, not only those Locus has (CR 602.2, 603.2); a mana ability is no trigger (CR 605.1a), nor is an
# opponent's activation. Bot1 crafts Locus on turn 7 (as in the crafting scenario: it has Mox Ruby's "{T}: Add {R}").
# On turn 8 Bot2 activates its Aether Spellbomb's "{1}, Sacrifice: Draw a card": one card, no copy (hand 7). On turn 9
# Bot1 taps Locus for {R} with the Mox Ruby ability it has - nothing goes on the stack - and spends it on its own
# Spellbomb's draw ability: Locus copies it, and Bot1 draws two (hand 1 -> 3, the Spellbomb cast from it first).

